     "text": "Davis-Bailey Clinic \nRe: Jacqueline Larson (DOB 04/05/1999) \n\n---\n\n**September 22, 2025:** \nJacqueline Larson, a 26-year-old female, presented to the clinic today for follow-up regarding her history of colon cancer. Her blood pressure was 134/91 and her weight was recorded at 114 pounds. During this visit, Ms. Larson reported no new symptoms or concerns. Her physical exam was unremarkable with no palpable lymphadenopathy and normal bowel sounds. The abdominal exam revealed no masses or tenderness. Ms. Larson is currently stable and doing well, with no signs of recurrence.\n\n**April 15, 2025:** \nToday, Jacqueline Larson returned for another follow-up related to her known colon cancer. Her blood pressure was 146/93 and her weight was 113 pounds. Ms. Larson has a history of stage III colon cancer, which she was diagnosed with approximately 10.4 years ago. Since completing her initial treatment regimen, she has remained in good health with no evidence of recurrence. Blood tests and imaging studies conducted during her last visit continue to show no abnormalities. She continues to manage her condition well with regular follow-ups and monitoring.\n\n**November 06, 2024:** \nJacqueline Larson visited the clinic today for a routine follow-up concerning her colon cancer. Her blood pressure was 142/90 and her weight was 114 pounds. Ms. Larson is doing well and reports no new symptoms. Her physical examination was within normal limits, with no palpable abnormalities. Lab results and imaging from the previous visit continue to show no signs of disease recurrence. Her overall health status remains stable and controlled.\n\n**May 29, 2024:** \nMs. Larson came in today primarily for a medication refill. Her blood pressure was 143/94 and her weight was 112 pounds. She has a history of stage colon cancer, diagnosed approximately 10.4 years ago. She has been in remission since her treatment and continues to do well. There were no new complaints or concerns during this visit. The examination was unremarkable, and her ongoing surveillance no signs of recurrence. \n\n**December 21, 2023:** \nJacqueline Larson was seen today for a lab review related to her history of colon cancer. Her blood pressure was 134/93 and her weight was 111 pounds. Ms. has been diagnosed with stage III colon cancer approximately 10.4 years ago. The latest lab results and imaging studies continue to show no evidence of disease recurrence. She remains asymptomatic and her physical was within normal limits. \n\n**July 13, 2023:** \nToday, Jacqueline Larson presented for a follow-up rela"
